window.CURRENT_TASK={"task_id": "L3-FUC-008-A6", "layer": "L3", "target_id": "FUC-008", "artifact_id": "FUC-008-A6", "title": "FUC-008 Resolve Dual Designations via Track Correlation / A6", "protocol_version": "L3_PURE_COVERAGE_3.0.0", "artifact_sha256": "8a5b74049f7d4a552a6283e2bf8ceaf5b3edc1f1c00b181275b2722feacbe0d9", "source_sha256": "40e0827f373b73731838c63950f540172969d6c83af6ebea4de3c9f3f5722e99", "reference_sha256": "920effdf5002dd8997c8a15ad01c9e30ecd8b6e396d6b3dacdd00bbe8c25ea3e", "reference_origin": "agent_reference_reused", "instructions": "<pre>本包明确复用冻结的 Agent 来源参照，属于人工覆盖复评，不构成“真人独立建立参照”。不展示任何候选评分。FULL为全部实质含义覆盖；PARTIAL不折半分；NOT_COVERED未覆盖；CONTRADICTED矛盾；UNRESOLVED未决。来源未决统一保留在分母，不能猜成已确认；技术失败另列且留在分母。允许七槽联合表达。</pre>", "material_html": "<h3>Resolve Dual Designations via Track Correlation</h3><p>给定参与者：C2 JU</p><div class=\"source\"><p>许可来源：milstd6016b_sec4</p><a href=\"assets/40e0827f373b73731838c63950f540172969d6c83af6ebea4de3c9f3f5722e99.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">打开完整来源 PDF（含原页图像）</a> · <a href=\"assets/40e0827f373b73731838c63950f540172969d6c83af6ebea4de3c9f3f5722e99.txt\" target=\"_blank\">同版全文文本</a></div><h3>冻结共同参照：已有 Agent 来源参照，非人工金标准</h3><pre>{&#x27;goal&#x27;: &#x27;Define requirements for a C2 JU to resolve real-time air and surface track dual designations through automatic and manual track correlation, J7.2 Correlation messages, reverse correlations/rejections, related J7.0 drop action, and associated correlation/decorrelation processing.&#x27;, &#x27;actor&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JU&#x27;, &#x27;start_boundary&#x27;: &#x27;When a C2 JU recognizes, tests, or is requested to correlate locally/remotely reported real-time air or surface tracks that may represent the same object or dual designation.&#x27;, &#x27;success_boundary&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU originates, receives, accepts, rejects, reverses, executes, abandons, or fails the correlation according to the specified tests, restrictions, timers, and Track Number/R2 actions; decorrelation processing is included where the source makes it part of common tracking and dual-designation handling.&#x27;, &#x27;in_scope&#x27;: [&#x27;Common tracking and correlation/decorrelation of local track data with received remote data&#x27;, &#x27;Automatic and manual air/surface track correlation&#x27;, &#x27;Periodic, receive-triggered, and pre-transmission correlation checks&#x27;, &#x27;J7.2 Correlation message origination and reception&#x27;, &#x27;Retained and Dropped Track Number selection&#x27;, &#x27;Response Values 0, 1, 2, and 3&#x27;, &#x27;Reverse correlation and correlation rejection&#x27;, &#x27;J7.0 Drop Track Report when the C2 JU has R2 for the dropped track&#x27;, &#x27;Correlation timing and position/course/speed/altitude tests&#x27;, &#x27;Correlation prohibitions, restrictions, parameter defaults, and two-test confirmation&#x27;, &#x27;Data retention or transfer upon execution of correlation&#x27;, &#x27;Automatic and manual decorrelation procedures supporting common tracking&#x27;, &#x27;Minimum waiting and filter constraints directly affecting correlation and resumption of track reporting&#x27;], &#x27;out_of_scope&#x27;: [&#x27;NonC2 JU transmission behavior on the Surveillance NPG&#x27;, &#x27;Point-to-point or point-to-track correlation using J7.2&#x27;, &#x27;Subsurface track correlation procedures&#x27;, &#x27;Ballistic missile track correlation, covariance encoding, and J7.1 ACT=2 update procedures&#x27;, &#x27;Land and space dual designation resolution, which is TBD in the supplied text&#x27;, &#x27;Electronic warfare LOB/fix correlation; only EW AOP rules explicitly involving J7.2 are outside this air/surface track target&#x27;], &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 113, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;4.7.3 RESOLUTION OF AIR AND SURFACE TRACK DUAL DESIGNATIONS&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;Section heading on PDF page 113&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 113, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;When a C2 JU recognizes that two tracks which are being reported to the interface are eligible for correlation, that JU shall initiate action, either automatically or manually, to resolve the dual designation. The recognizing JU shall transmit the J7.2 Correlation message requesting all other C2 IUs to perform a correlation of the two tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 25, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;all C2 JUs shall perform correlation and decorrelation of their local track data with respect to the remote data which they are receiving. Failure to properly correlate can result in a dual designation.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 25, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;All C2 JUs that originate real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic correlation capability.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 39, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;All C2 JUs that initiate real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic decorrelation capability.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre><h3>交互目标 / goal</h3><pre>[goal:0 / CL-4d234a6281e32704] To recognize and resolve air and surface track dual designations by having a C2 JU initiate track correlation, transmit a J7.2 Correlation message requesting other C2 IUs to perform correlation of the two tracks, and identify the TN to be retained and the TN to be dropped.</pre><h3>前置条件 / preconditions</h3><pre>[preconditions:0 / CL-6472314995e293b7 / step 1] Two tracks are being reported to the interface and are eligible for correlation.</pre><pre>[preconditions:1 / CL-b02230201d17f45f / step 2] The dual designation is for air or surface tracks; the rules for land (ground) and space track dual designation resolution are TBD.</pre><pre>[preconditions:2 / CL-43b678c9baf45815 / step 3] The C2 JU has the capability to perform common tracking in accordance with the correlation and decorrelation procedures and criteria.</pre><pre>[preconditions:3 / CL-bbc9684c0a3c23f5 / step 4] The C2 JU has an automatic correlation capability for real-time air or surface tracks it originates.</pre><h3>触发条件 / trigger</h3><pre>[trigger:0 / CL-bce0ea54b4335b32] When a C2 JU recognizes that two tracks which are being reported to the interface are eligible for correlation, it initiates action, either automatically or manually, to resolve the dual designation.</pre><h3>主流程 / main_flow</h3><pre>[main_flow:0 / CL-64c8c761603a9dfb / step 1] All IUs periodically compare remote tracks to local tracks (and, optionally, to common local tracks) to determine if a dual designation has occurred.</pre><pre>[main_flow:1 / CL-0baf7b71ac42ad99 / step 2] All C2 JUs perform correlation and decorrelation of their local track data with respect to the remote data which they are receiving; the correlation process commences with comparing locally derived sensor data (position, velocity, and altitude) with the data received on the interface, in order to prevent or eliminate dual designations.</pre><pre>[main_flow:2 / CL-7d7590f45fcc6914 / step 3] When a C2 JU recognizes that two tracks which are being reported to the interface are eligible for correlation, that JU initiates action, either automatically or manually, to resolve the dual designation.</pre><pre>[main_flow:3 / CL-e57f7e5a4a000613 / step 4] The recognizing JU transmits the J7.2 Correlation message requesting all other C2 IUs to perform a correlation of the two tracks.</pre><pre>[main_flow:4 / CL-c7ca3ab1394e589d / step 5] The J7.2 Correlation message identifies the TN to be retained and the TN to be dropped, and the originating JU indicates in the message if it has any constraint which would prohibit accepting a reverse correlation.</pre><pre>[main_flow:5 / CL-e4c3371272763753 / step 6] C2 JUs shall not automatically select as the TN to be dropped a TN which has any of the OCCs listed in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1g(6 7); in the absence of such a selection constraint, JUs shall select the higher TN as the TN to be dropped.</pre><pre>[main_flow:6 / CL-3c4b4f551588e2a0 / step 7] Receiving IUs accept the requested correlation unless certain prespecified conditions exist which require or allow the receiving IU to reject the requested correlation or respond with a reverse correlation request.</pre><pre>[main_flow:7 / CL-53f656fcba0f943e / step 8] Two tracks shall pass the correlation tests and restrictions twice before the correlation is executed; when they pass once they are deemed a tentative correlation, are tested again upon the next correlation stimulus, and, if they pass the second correlation test with no correlation restriction, are processed for dual designation resolution in accordance with paragraphs 4.4.4.3.1j and k.</pre><h3>备选流程 / alternative_flow</h3><pre>[alternative_flow:0 / CL-cdedc767ab2a0355 / step 6] If prespecified conditions exist that require or allow rejection of the requested correlation, the receiving IU rejects the correlation and transmits the J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2 to report the rejection.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:1 / CL-ce24d1f01e80ffba / step 6] If a receiving IU desires to reverse the requested correlation, it uses the RV field to determine if a reverse correlation request should be originated or if the original correlation request should be rejected; RV value 0 indicates a reverse correlation would be acceptable, and RV value 1 indicates a reverse correlation request would be rejected.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:2 / CL-f516d4fe1d3b119c / step 6] If the RV field is set to value 3, the correlation was manually initiated and shall be accepted unless certain conditions apply which require rejection.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:3 / CL-68e8176471d743e6 / step 7] If the Retained TN and the Dropped TN will decorrelate when subjected to the decorrelation criteria once, the correlation shall be rejected.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:4 / CL-89892f47f5a3fcfd / step 6] If there is an OCC on the Dropped TN and the received RV field is set to value 0, the reverse correlation shall be transmitted if the new Dropped TN has no correlation constraint; if both the Retained TN and Dropped TN have an OCC, the correlation shall be rejected.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:5 / CL-91620cbd369f8335 / step 6] If there is an OCC on the Dropped TN and the received RV field is set to value 1, the correlation shall be rejected.</pre><pre>[alternative_flow:6 / CL-739090c5875805e8 / step 7] If the above actions result in resolution of the ID conflict, the TN to be retained shall be tested for decorrelation in accordance with paragraph 4.4.4.3.2a before executing the correlation, except the test shall be conducted only once.</pre><h3>异常流程 / exception_flow</h3><pre>[exception_flow:0 / CL-21923a495ecb92ca / step 1] If the dual designation involves land (ground) or space tracks, the rules for land (ground) and space track dual designation resolution are TBD; exit the exception path with no resolution procedure specified for those tracks.</pre><pre>[exception_flow:1 / CL-18cec76d31247d9c / step 2] If prespecified conditions require or allow a receiving IU to reject the requested correlation, the receiving IU rejects the correlation and transmits the J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2 to report the rejection; exit with the correlation request rejected.</pre><pre>[exception_flow:2 / CL-cea8a8544fe494d9 / step 3] If a receiving IU desires to reverse the requested correlation, it uses the RV field to determine whether to originate a reverse correlation request or reject the original correlation request: RV value 0 indicates a reverse correlation would be acceptable, and RV value 1 indicates a reverse correlation request would be rejected; exit by originating a reverse correlation request (RV=0) or by rejecting the original correlation request and transmitting the J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2 to report the rejection (RV=1).</pre><pre>[exception_flow:3 / CL-765541474b7754e2 / step 4] If the RV field is set to value 3, the correlation was manually initiated and shall be accepted unless certain conditions apply which require rejection; if such a condition applies, reject the correlation and transmit the J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2 to report the rejection; exit with the correlation accepted or the rejection reported.</pre><h3>后置条件 / postconditions</h3><pre>[postconditions:0 / CL-cfcd7afdca5e4538 / step 1] A J7.2 Correlation message has been transmitted by the recognizing C2 JU requesting all other C2 IUs to perform a correlation of the two tracks.</pre><pre>[postconditions:1 / CL-78eacbd28e97c931 / step 2] The J7.2 Correlation message identifies the TN to be retained and the TN to be dropped.</pre><pre>[postconditions:2 / CL-ba91fbb2bf3aa520 / step 3] The receiving C2 IUs have accepted the requested correlation.</pre><pre>[postconditions:3 / CL-acbaf526a97e3f57 / step 4] The two tracks have successfully passed the correlation tests and restrictions twice with no correlation restriction, and the correlation has been executed.</pre><pre>[postconditions:4 / CL-629ea3642aadd2f9 / step 5] The TN to be dropped was not automatically selected from a TN having any of the OCCs listed in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1g(6 7); absent such a selection constraint, the higher TN was selected as the TN to be dropped.</pre><pre>[postconditions:5 / CL-54493287944eb455 / step 6] For the track corresponding to the dropped TN, the C2 JU has ceased reporting the track and has transmitted a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message on the surveillance TN.</pre>", "groups": [{"key": "coverage", "title": "逐需求覆盖", "fields": [{"key": "label", "label": "覆盖标签", "type": "select", "required": true, "options": ["FULL", "PARTIAL", "NOT_COVERED", "CONTRADICTED", "UNRESOLVED", "TECHNICAL_FAILURE"]}, {"key": "location", "label": "输出位置/断言 ID/原文；无匹配填无", "type": "textarea", "required": true}, {"key": "reason", "label": "判定理由（列出遗漏的条件、否定、顺序或结果）", "type": "textarea", "required": true}], "rows": [{"title": "S16-02-R0001", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall perform correlation and decorrelation of its local track data with respect to the remote data it receives; a C2 JU capable of originating and reporting real-time air, surface, land, or space tracks shall have a common-tracking capability, with air and surface procedures governing this target.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 25, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;all C2 JUs shall perform correlation and decorrelation of their local track data with respect to the remote data which they are receiving.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 25, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Each C2 JU which has a capability to originate and report real-time air, surface (maritime), land (ground), or space tracks shall have a capability to perform common tracking&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0002", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU that originates real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic correlation capability.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 25, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;All C2 JUs that originate real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic correlation capability.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0003", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall periodically compare remote tracks to local tracks, and optionally common local tracks, using the frequency, same-object criteria, and correlation rules in section 4.4.4.3.1 to determine whether an air or surface dual designation occurred; land and space dual-designation rules are TBD.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 113, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The recognition and resolution of dual designations require all IUs to periodically compare remote tracks to local tracks (and, optionally, to common local tracks) to determine if a dual designation has occurred. The frequency of such comparisons the criteria for determining that two tracks represent the same object, and the correlation rules shall be in accordance with section 4.4.4.3.1&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 113, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The rules for land (ground) and space track dual designation resolution are TBD.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0004", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When a C2 JU recognizes two tracks reported to the interface as eligible for correlation, it shall initiate automatic or manual action to resolve the dual designation and shall transmit a J7.2 Correlation message identifying the TN to be retained and the TN to be dropped.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 113, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;When a C² JU recognizes that two tracks which are being reported to the interface are eligible for correlation, that JU shall initiate action, either automatically or manually, to resolve the dual designation. The recognizing JU shall transmit the J7.2 Correlation message requesting all other C² IUs to perform a correlation of the two tracks. The message identifies the TN to be retained and the TN to be dropped.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0005", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU capable of reporting air or surface tracks shall be capable of transmitting and receiving all J7.2 response values for real-time air and/or surface tracks held locally by its system.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 113, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;All C² JUs capable of reporting air or surface tracks shall have the capability to transmit and receive all the response values of the J7.2 message for real-time air and/or surface tracks, which are held locally by their system.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0006", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall make an automatic correlation test upon receipt of each unconfirmed remote real-time J3.2/J3.3 track or eligible J2.0/J2.2/J2.3 PPLI report, comparing the received remote track or IU with local tracks of the same E/C, including previously common local tracks for which own unit has R2.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;trigger&quot;:&quot;Receipt of an unconfirmed eligible remote real-time track or PPLI report&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 26, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Upon receipt of each remote real-time J3.2 or J3.3 track or J2.0 (Originator E/C = 0 or 3), J2.2, or J2.3 PPLI report which is not confirmed to have an existing correlation to a local track. Such tests shall compare the received remote track or IU to local tracks of the same E/C, including previously common local tracks for which own unit has R².&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;Automatic Correlation paragraph in the lower half of received page 26&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0007", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;Alternatively, a C2 JU shall make an automatic correlation test immediately prior to each local-track transmission, comparing the local track with remote tracks and IUs of the same E/C.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;trigger&quot;:&quot;Immediately before transmission of a local track&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 26, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Immediately prior to each transmission of a local track. Such tests shall compare the local track to remote tracks and IUs of the same E/C.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;Alternative Automatic Correlation rule on received page 26&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0008", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not report a new local track to the interface until automatic correlation has been attempted and failed on the initial test, or on the next test after an initial tentative correlation; if no tentative correlation is found initially, the track shall be transmitted, and if tentative correlation is followed by failure, it shall be transmitted.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 26, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;New local tracks shall not be reported to the interface until an automatic correlation has been attempted and failed on an initial correlation test or on the next test following an initial tentative correlation (see paragraph 4.4.4.3.1h). If no tentative correlation is found on the initial test, the new local track shall be transmitted. If the new local track tentatively correlates on the initial test but fails correlation on the next test, the new local track shall be transmitted.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0009", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A new local track that correlates with another track on each of the first two correlation tests shall be correlated and held as a common local track, after which decorrelation rules apply.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 26, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;A new local track that correlates with another track on each of the first two correlation tests shall be correlated and held as a common local track. Thereafter, the decorrelation rules (see paragraph 4.4.4.3.2) apply to the track.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0010", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;Correlation tests performed by a C2 JU shall include active IUs, remote real-time tracks, and other local tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 26, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Correlation tests shall include active IUs, remote real-time tracks, and other local tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0011", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If operator action selectively releases a new local track for reporting, the C2 JU shall transmit it regardless of correlation-test results.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;operator_action&quot;:&quot;selective release of a new local track for reporting&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 26, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If an operator action has been taken which selectively released a new local track for reporting, it shall be transmitted, regardless of the results of correlation testing.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0012", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall provide a manual capability to initiate correlation of any two tracks irrespective of automatic test criteria, restrictions, or new-track requirements, except it shall not manually correlate tracks of different E/C, a simulated track with a live track, or two remote tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 27, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;A manual capability shall be provided to initiate the correlation of any two tracks irrespective of the correlation test criteria in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1f, the correlation restrictions in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1g, or the requirements in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1h, except that two tracks shall not be manually correlated if they are of a different E/C, or one is simulated and the other is live, or both are remote.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0013", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall perform correlation tests in response to correlation requests from other units in accordance with paragraph 4.7.3.2.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;trigger&quot;:&quot;Receives a correlation request from another unit&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 27, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JUs shall perform correlation tests in response to correlation requests from other units in accordance with the requirements of paragraph 4.7.3.2.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0014", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;For correlation testing, a C2 JU shall extrapolate positions of all tested tracks and IUs to the same time, perform the correlation test no more than 6 seconds after the extrapolation time, and consider a local track correlated only to the closest remote track or IU that passes all tests and satisfies restrictions and the two-test requirement.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 27, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Positions of all tracks and IUs tested for correlation shall be extrapolated to the same time. The correlation test shall occur no more than 6 seconds after the extrapolation time. A local track shall be considered to correlate to the closest remote track or IU that meets all of the correlation tests, subject to the correlation restrictions in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1g and the requirement to pass two correlation tests in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1h.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0015", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall use the positional test D ≤ [a*SQRT(L2+R2)+b] dm to determine positional eligibility, subject to the other tests, prohibitions, and limitations.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 30, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Two tracks shall be eligible for correlation, subject to the other tests, prohibitions, and limitations of this paragraph, if they pass the following positional test:&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 31, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;D ≤ [a*SQRT(L2 + R2) + b] dm&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0016", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When both tracks have speed at least 10 dmh, a C2 JU shall apply the course differential test MIN(|CR-CL|, 360-|CR-CL|) ≤ f; otherwise course shall not be used.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;speed_condition&quot;:&quot;both tracks have speed ≥ 10 dmh&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 28, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If both tracks have speed ≥ 10 dmh:&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 28, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;MIN(|CR-CL|, 360-|CR-CL|) ≤ f&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 28, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Otherwise course is not used in the correlation test.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0017", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall apply the speed differential test |1-SS/SF| X 100% ≤ MAX(g,[g(k/SF)]), using k=200 dmh for air tracks and k=20 dmh for surface tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 28, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Speed Test |1-SS/SF| X 100% ≤ MAX(g,[g(k/SF)])&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 28, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;= 200 dmh for air tracks; = 20 dmh for surface tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0018", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;For air tracks, a C2 JU shall apply the altitude test |AR-AL| ≤ h when both tracks have Altitude Source 1 or 3, or when the local track has Altitude Source 1 or 3 and the remote track is an IU reported in PPLI; otherwise altitude shall not be used.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;air_track&quot;:true}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 28, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;For air tracks, if both tracks have an Altitude Source = 1 or 3, or if the local track Altitude Source is 1 or 3 and the remote track is an IU reported in a PPLI message: |AR-AL| ≤ h&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 28, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Otherwise altitude is not used in the correlation test.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0019", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not automatically test tracks with TQ ≤ e, JUs with Qpg=0, tracks of different E/C, tracks with existing E/C conflicts, simulated tracks against live tracks, or live tracks against simulated tracks; the TQ/Qpg prohibition does not apply to new local real-time tracks but does apply to nonreal-time TQ=0 tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 29, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The following shall not be tested for correlation: (a) A track with TQ ≤ e (see paragraph 4.4.4.3.1f(2)), or a JU with Qpg = 0 (see paragraph 4.4.4.3.1f(8)(b)). This prohibition does not apply to new local real-time tracks, but does apply to nonreal-time (TQ=0) tracks. (b) Tracks of different E/C, and tracks with existing E/C conflicts. (c) Simulated tracks with live tracks, and live tracks with simulated tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0020", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall support variable correlation parameters at initialization using any value in the specified ranges and increments, and shall set each parameter to its default when no other value is specified; default values are the same for air and surface correlation, but actual air and surface values may differ.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 29, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Systems shall be capable of using any value within the specified range and increments upon system initialization, and shall set the parameter to the default value if no other value is specified. The default values are the same for air and surface track correlation. However, the actual value to be used for air tracks may be specified differently than that used for surface tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0021", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When calculating correlation windows, a C2 JU shall treat TQs less than c as TQ c and TQs greater than d as TQ d; tracks with TQ less than or equal to e shall not be automatically correlated.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 31, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Tracks with TQ less than or equal to the restricted TQ value e shall not be automatically correlated&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 32, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;TQs less than c shall be treated the same as TQ c, and TQs greater than d shall be treated the same as d, for purposes of calculating D, the correlation window.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0022", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;For J2.2 Air or J2.3 Surface PPLI correlation, a C2 JU shall use the maximum positional error associated with the remote Geodetic Position Quality as R, treating Qpg below j as j and Qpg above k as k.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;remote_report&quot;:&quot;J2.2 Air or J2.3 Surface PPLI&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 33, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;When the remote report being tested for correlation is a J2.2 Air or J2.3 Surface PPLI message, the maximum positional error associated with the reported Geodetic Position Quality (Qpg) shall be used for the value of R in the position test. Qpg less than j shall be treated as Qpg = j, and Qpg greater than k shall be treated as Qpg = k.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0023", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If a received J2.2 or J2.3 has Qpg=0, the C2 JU shall not automatically correlate it, except that when Qpg=0 is received for a JU held as a common local track, R2 may be assumed under paragraph 4.4.2.2.2d.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;qpg&quot;:0}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 33, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If the received J2.2 or J2.3 Qpg = 0, the PPLI shall not be correlated automatically. However, if a J2.2 or J2.3 with Qpg = 0 is received for a JU held as a common local track, R2 for the common local track may be assumed in accordance with paragraph 4.4.2.2.2d.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0024", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall process a J2.0 Indirect PPLI with Originator E/C 0 or 3 for correlation like a J3.3 surface track or J3.2 air track, respectively, with TQ=7.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;remote_report&quot;:&quot;J2.0 Indirect PPLI with Originator E/C 0 or 3&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 34, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;When the remote report being tested for correlation is a J2.0 Indirect PPLI message with the Originator E/C field set to value 0 (Surface) or 3 (Air), it shall be processed for correlation like a J3.2 air or J3.3 surface (maritime) track with TQ = 7.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0025", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not automatically correlate two tracks that pass the tests when an identity conflict exists, and shall provide initialization and operator-selectable capabilities to inhibit this restriction; absent specific interface direction, identity-conflict restriction shall apply by default.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;restriction&quot;:&quot;identity difference constitutes a conflict&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 34, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The two tracks have an Identity (ID) difference which constitutes a conflict (see paragraph 4.4.4.3.1i). Systems shall have an initialization parameter and an operator selectable capability to inhibit this automatic restriction.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 34, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;In lieu of specific interface direction, all IUs will restrict automatic correlation by default.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0026", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not automatically correlate tracks with different Mode II codes when the local Mode II code is current, and shall provide initialization and operator-selectable capabilities to inhibit this restriction; the restriction shall apply by default absent interface direction.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;restriction&quot;:&quot;different Mode II codes and local Mode II code current&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 34, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The two tracks have different Mode II codes, and the local Mode II code is current. Systems shall have an initialization parameter and an operator selectable capability to inhibit this automatic restriction.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 34, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;In lieu of specific interface direction, all IUs will restrict automatic correlation by default.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0027", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not automatically correlate two locally derived real-time tracks being updated with local positional data.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;restriction&quot;:&quot;both tracks locally derived real-time tracks&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 34, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Both tracks are locally derived real-time tracks, i.e., being updated with local positional data.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0028", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not automatically correlate tracks when either track has Strength greater than 1; if either Strength is No Statement, the C2 JU shall not inhibit correlation for this restriction.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;restriction&quot;:&quot;either track Strength &gt; 1&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 34, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Either track has the Strength field set to a value greater than 1. Systems shall not inhibit correlation if either track has Strength set to No Statement.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0029", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not automatically correlate a common local track with a remote track when the same unit has R2 for both tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;restriction&quot;:&quot;same unit has R2 for common local and remote tracks&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 35, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;One track is a common local track and the other is a remote, and the same unit has R² for both tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0030", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not automatically correlate either track if it is currently subject to a dual designation resolution action involving another TN.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;restriction&quot;:&quot;track subject to another dual designation resolution action&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 35, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Either track is currently the subject of a dual designation resolution action involving another TN.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0031", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not automatically correlate tracks when each is subject to one or more operational contingency constraints, including current engagement status, pending command or mission assignment requiring reply, control by a J10.5 report, or active/inactive IU status.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;restriction&quot;:&quot;each track is subject to one or more OCCs&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 35, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Each track is subject to one or more (not necessarily the same) of the below operational contingency constraints (OCC).&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 35, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The TN is the subject of a current engagement status message&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 35, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The TN is the subject of a pending J9.0 Command message&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 35, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The TN is currently a controlled track&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 35, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The TN is an active or inactive IU.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0032", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU may apply one exception to the identity-conflict and current-engagement restrictions if the unit attempting correlation originated a J10.2 where its target has Unknown or Hostile ID and the other track has Friend ID; the Unknown/Hostile track shall be the dropped TN, and this exception shall not be applied upon receipt of a J7.2 Correlation message.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;exception&quot;:&quot;unit attempting correlation originated J10.2 and target is Unknown/Hostile while other is Friend&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 35, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If either subject track is the Target TN in a J10.2 Engagement Status message originated by the unit attempting correlation, and that track has an ID of Unknown or Hostile, and the other subject track has an ID of Friend, then automatic correlation may be allowed. The Unknown/Hostile track shall be the dropped Track Number (TN-2).&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 35, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;This exception shall not be applied by any JU upon receipt of a J7.2 Correlation message.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0033", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU receiving a J7.2 while holding OCCs on both tracks or conflicting IDs with the ID-conflict restriction enabled shall reject the correlation under paragraph 4.7.3.2a(1).&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;trigger&quot;:&quot;Receipt of J7.2 with both-track OCCs or enabled ID conflict&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 35, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Thus, any JU receiving a J7.2 Correlation message and also holding OCCs on both tracks or conflicting IDs on the two tracks (if the ID conflict correlation restriction is enabled (see paragraph 4.4.4.3.1g(1)) shall reject the correlation in accordance with paragraph 4.7.3.2a(1).&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0034", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;Two tracks shall pass the correlation tests and restrictions 2(1-2,1) times before correlation is executed; one successful pass shall create a tentative correlation, the same pair shall be retested at the next stimulus, and a second successful pass with no restriction shall lead to dual-designation resolution processing.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 36, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Two tracks shall pass the correlation tests and restrictions in paragraphs 4.4.4.3.1f and 4.4.4.3.1g 2(1-2,1) times before the correlation is executed. When two tracks pass the correlation tests and restrictions once, they shall be deemed a tentative correlation. The same two tracks shall be tested again upon the next correlation stimulus (see paragraph 4.4.4.3.1c). If the two tracks successfully pass the second correlation test and there is no correlation restriction, they shall be processed for dual designation resolution&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0035", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall treat tracks as having conflicting IDs for correlation processing when Table 4.7-2 indicates code 1, or code 1* that the system processes as a conflict except Hostile versus Pending, or when Exercise Indicators differ.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 36, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Two tracks shall be considered to have conflicting IDs for correlation processing if: (a) The ID difference is indicated by the code &quot;1&quot; in Table 4.7-2. (b) The ID difference is indicated by the code &quot;1*&quot; in Table 4.7-2 and the system processes these differences as conflicts, except that Hostile vs. Pending shall not be considered a conflict for correlation processing. (c) One track has the Exercise Indicator set to value 0 and the other has it set to value 1.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0036", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If conflicting IDs is the only correlation restriction, the C2 JU shall alert the operator to change local ID or Exercise Indicator and ID, transmit an ID Difference Report, confirm the restriction, or conduct voice coordination.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;only_restriction&quot;:&quot;conflicting IDs&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 36, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If conflicting IDs is the only correlation restriction, the operator shall be alerted. The purpose of this alert is to cue the operator to take one of the following actions: (a) Change the local ID or the Exercise Indicator and ID, thereby allowing automatic correlation, or (b) Transmit an ID Difference Report, thereby allowing automatic correlation if the remote ID or Exercise Indicator and ID is changed, or (c) Confirm the restriction, thereby inhibiting the correlation, or (d) Conduct voice coordination to resolve the situation.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0037", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If actions resolve an ID conflict, the C2 JU shall test the TN to be retained for decorrelation once before executing the correlation.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;prerequisite&quot;:&quot;ID conflict resolved&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 37, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If the above actions result in resolution of the ID conflict, the TN to be retained shall be tested for decorrelation in accordance with paragraph 4.4.4.3.2a before executing the correlation, except the test shall be conducted only once.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0038", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not automatically select a TN with any listed OCC as the dropped TN; absent such a constraint, it shall select the higher TN as dropped, using the TN greater than 07777 for comparison when a track has both representations in a J7.4 message.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 37, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JUs shall not automatically select as the TN to be dropped a TN which has any of the OCCs listed in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1g(6 7). In the absence of such a selection constraint, JUs shall select the higher TN as the TN to be dropped. For a track that has both a TN greater than 07777 and a TN less than 07777, as reported in a J7.4 message, the track with TN greater than 07777 shall be used in this comparison.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0039", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If no J7.0 ACT=0 is received for the dropped TN within 60 seconds after transmission of the correlation request, the C2 JU shall deem the correlation failed and cancel all associated correlation processing.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;timeout&quot;:&quot;60 seconds without J7.0 ACT=0 for dropped TN&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 37, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The correlation shall be deemed to have failed if no J7.0 (ACT = 0) is received for the dropped TN after a period of 60 seconds from the transmission of the correlation request and all associated processing for the correlation shall be cancelled.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0040", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If own unit holds the Dropped TN as a local or common local track, the C2 JU shall designate the Retained TN as a common local track.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 37, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If own unit holds the Dropped TN as a local or common local track, the Retained TN shall be designated as a common local track.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0041", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If the C2 JU has R2 for the Dropped TN, it shall transmit a J7.0 ACT=0 Drop Track message for that TN; if another IU reports the Dropped TN afterward, the C2 JU shall retain it as remote and shall not reattempt correlation between Retained and Dropped TNs for 60 seconds after the J7.0 transmission.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;r2_for_dropped&quot;:true}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 37, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If own unit has R² for the Dropped TN, a J7.0 (ACT = 0) Drop Track message shall be transmitted for the Dropped TN. If the Dropped TN is reported by another IU after transmission of the J7.0, own unit shall retain the Dropped TN as a remote track and shall not reattempt to correlate the Retained TN and the Dropped TN for a period of 60 seconds after transmission of the J7.0.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0042", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When own unit initiates a J7.2 and no Drop Track message has yet been received for the Dropped TN, the C2 JU shall retain it as a remote track.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 38, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;When a J7.2 message is initiated by own unit and a Drop Track message has not yet been received for the Dropped TN, it shall be retained as a remote track.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0043", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;Upon execution of correlation, the C2 JU shall transfer the Dropped TN kinematic data—Latitude, Longitude, Course, Speed, Altitude, Altitude Source, TQ, and Strength—to the Retained TN when the Dropped TN is a local or common local track, and shall transfer no other Dropped TN data outside the specified categories.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 38, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Data specified below shall be transferred from the Dropped TN to the Retained TN when the correlation is executed. No other Dropped TN data shall be transferred to the Retained TN.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 38, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If the Dropped TN is a local or common local track, the Dropped TN Latitude, Longitude, Course, Speed, Altitude, Altitude Source, TQ, and Strength shall be transferred to the Retained TN.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0044", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When the identity-conflict restriction is not inhibited and Table 4.7-2 would automatically accept the Dropped TN ID/IAD, the C2 JU shall transfer the Dropped TN ID/IAD and Special Interest Indicator, Platform, Platform Activity, and Specific Type to the Retained TN.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;id_restriction_state&quot;:&quot;not inhibited&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 38, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Restriction Not Inhibited: If the Identity (ID) (or Identity Amplifying Descriptor (IAD) of two exercise tracks) of retained TN and Dropped TN are different and the difference would result in automatic acceptance of the Dropped TN ID/IAD in accordance with Table 4.7-2, the Dropped TN ID/IAD and Special Interest Indicator, Platform, Platform Activity, and Specific Type shall be transferred to Retained TN.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0045", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When the identity-conflict restriction is inhibited, the C2 JU shall retain reported identification data when identities are the same; when identities differ, it shall treat the last Dropped TN Identity as equivalent to a J7.0 ACT=1 Identity Difference Report and process it under paragraph 4.7.1.2.2 immediately after correlation.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;id_restriction_state&quot;:&quot;inhibited&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 38, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Restriction Inhibited: When the Identity of Retained TN and Dropped TN are the same, associated identification data (Platform, Platform Activity, Specific Type, Exercise Indicator, and Special Interest Indicator) reported for the Retained TN shall be retained. When the Identity of Retained TN and Dropped TN are different, the last Identity reported for Dropped TN shall be considered equivalent to a J7.0 (ACT = 1) Identity Difference Report for the Retained TN. It shall be processed in accordance with paragraph 4.7.1.2.2 immediately after the correlation is executed.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0046", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;The C2 JU shall transfer nonzero Dropped TN Mode I, II, or III IFF/SIF data to the Retained TN for any mode where Retained TN data is zero, and shall transfer higher Dropped TN Mode IV data.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 38, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Any Dropped TN nonzero Mode I, II, or III IFF/SIF data for a mode for which the Retained TN data is zero shall be transferred to the Retained TN. If the Dropped TN Mode IV data is a higher value than the Retained TN Mode IV data, it shall be transferred to the Retained TN.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0047", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If the Dropped TN had Force Tell Indicator 1 or Emergency Indicator 1, the C2 JU shall set the corresponding indicator on the Retained TN.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 39, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If the Dropped TN had the Force Tell Indicator set to value 1, the Retained TN shall have the Force Tell Indicator set to value 1. If the Dropped TN had the Emergency Indicator set to value 1, the Retained TN shall have the Emergency Indicator set to value 1.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0048", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU that initiates real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic decorrelation capability and may perform manual decorrelation or require manual confirmation of automatic decorrelations.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 39, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;All C2 JUs that initiate real-time air or surface tracks shall have an automatic decorrelation capability. C2 JUs may also perform manual decorrelation, and may have a capability to require manual confirmation of automatic decorrelations.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0049", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall perform automatic decorrelation tests for each common local track upon receipt of each J2 or J3 message on that track.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;trigger&quot;:&quot;Receives each J2 or J3 message on a common local track&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 39, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Automatic decorrelation tests shall be performed for each common local track upon receipt of each J2 or J3 message on the track.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0050", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall decorrelate a common local track when 2(1-5,1) consecutive remote reports place the remote track outside 1.5(1.0-2.0,0.1) times the maximum correlation distance.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 39, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Common local tracks shall be decorrelated if, on receipt of 2(1-5, 1) consecutive remote track reports, the remote track falls outside a distance of 1.5(1.0-2.0, 0.1) times the maximum correlation distance calculated in accordance with paragraph 4.4.4.3.1f(3).&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0051", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;After decorrelation criteria are met, the C2 JU shall automatically test the local track once for correlation against remote tracks that are not common local tracks; if the test fails, it shall assign a new TN and report it in J3.2/J3.3 with initial ID Pending, except manual decorrelation may allow operator override of Pending.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 39, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The local track shall be automatically tested once for correlation against remote tracks (not common local tracks) in accordance with paragraphs 4.4.4.3.1f and g. If the automatic correlation test fails, assign a new TN (TN B) to the local track and report TN B in a J3.2 or J3.3 message, with an initial ID of Pending. For manual decorrelation the Pending ID may be overridden by operator action.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0052", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;After executing decorrelation, the C2 JU shall establish TN A as a remote track.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 40, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;(2) Establish TN A as a remote track.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0053", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When decorrelating a track with engagement, pending-command, control, pairing, index-number, or handover OCCs, the C2 JU shall take the specified decorrelation, delay, alert, message-update, display, or assessment action for that OCC.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 40, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If local or remote data held indicates one of the following conditions exist, action shall be taken as indicated:&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 40, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Decorrelate and alert an operator as a cue to transmit the J10.2 message with the Weapon Engagement Status field set to value 8 (Engagement Broken) if appropriate.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 40, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Do not automatically decorrelate.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 41, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The decorrelation shall be delayed until the handover process is completed or terminated&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0054", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;When originating a J7.2 for a dual designation, the C2 JU shall set RV=0 when the Retained TN has no OCC, RV=1 when the Retained TN has an OCC, and RV=3 when correlation was manually initiated.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 114, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The RV field shall be set to: value 0 if there is no OCC on the Retained TN. value 1 if the Retained TN has an OCC. value 3 if the correlation was manually initiated.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0055", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If a selection conflict occurs because OCCs exist on both Retained and Dropped TN, the C2 JU shall abandon correlation until the next correlation check.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;selection_conflict&quot;:&quot;OCCs on both TNs&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 114, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If a selection conflict occurs due to OCCs on both the Retained TN and the Dropped TN the correlation shall be abandoned until the next correlation check.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0056", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;After the C2 JU originates a J7.2 with RV 0 or 1 and receives a J7.2 containing one or both of the same TNs, it shall discontinue transmission of its J7.2.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 114, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;Transmission of a J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 0 or 1 shall be discontinued upon receipt of a J7.2 message containing one or both of the same TNs.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0057", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If the originating C2 JU holds R2 for the Dropped TN, it shall drop that TN and transmit J7.0 ACT=0 after the J7.2 message.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;r2_for_dropped&quot;:true}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 114, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If the originating C2 JU holds R² for the Dropped TN, it shall drop the Dropped TN and transmit the J7.0 (ACT = 0) message. The J7.0 (ACT = 0) message shall be transmitted after the J7.2 message.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0058", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU capable of transmitting J7.2 shall provide an operator-selectable capability to deactivate automatic J7.2 transmission.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 114, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JUs capable of transmitting the J7.2 message shall have an operator selectable capability to deactivate automatic transmission of the message.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0059", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU receiving J7.2 with RV 0 or 1 shall not accept the requested correlation when a correlation restriction listed in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1g exists and shall reject it.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;rv&quot;:&quot;0 or 1&quot;,&quot;restriction&quot;:&quot;correlation restriction listed in 4.4.4.3.1g&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 114, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JUs receiving a J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 0 or 1 shall not accept the requested correlation when local or remote data held indicates one or more of the following conditions exist: (1) There is a correlation restriction as listed in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1g. In this case the correlation shall be rejected.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0060", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If a single decorrelation-criteria check shows the Retained and Dropped TNs would decorrelate, the C2 JU shall reject the requested correlation.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 115, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The Retained TN and the Dropped TN will decorrelate, i.e., when subjected to the decorrelation criteria once, the tracks would decorrelate. In this case the correlation shall be rejected.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0061", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If the Dropped TN has an OCC and received RV=0, the C2 JU shall transmit a reverse correlation when the new Dropped TN has no constraint; if both TNs have OCCs, it shall reject the correlation.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;rv&quot;:0,&quot;dropped_tn_occ&quot;:true}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 115, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;There is an OCC on the Dropped TN as listed in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1g(7) and the received RV field is set to value 0. The reverse correlation shall be transmitted if the new Dropped TN has no correlation constraint. If both the Retained TN and Dropped TN have an OCC, the correlation shall be rejected.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0062", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If the Dropped TN has an OCC and received RV=1, the C2 JU shall reject the correlation.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;rv&quot;:1,&quot;dropped_tn_occ&quot;:true}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 115, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;There is an OCC on the Dropped TN as listed in paragraph 4.4.4.3.1g(7) and the received RV field is set to value 1. In this case the correlation shall be rejected.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0063", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;After receiving or generating J7.2 RV=2 Correlation Rejection, a C2 JU shall not automatically originate a request with the same Retained/Dropped TN pair for 2(1-10,1) minutes; a rejected manual correlation originator shall alert the operator as a cue for voice coordination, while an automatic-rejection alert is a system option.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 115, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JUs receiving or generating a J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 2, Correlation Rejection, shall not automatically originate a request with the same Retained TN and Dropped TN for a period of 2(1-10,1) minutes. When a correlation request is rejected for a manual correlation, the JU originating the request shall provide an operator alert as a cue to conduct voice coordination. An operator alert in the event of the rejection of an automatic correlation shall be a system option.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0064", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU receiving J7.2 RV=3 shall automatically accept the manually initiated correlation unless tracks differ in E/C, either has an E/C conflict, one is simulated and the other live, or both are locally derived real-time tracks; in those cases it shall reject.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;rv&quot;:3}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 115, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JUs receiving a J7.2 message with the RV field set to value 3 shall automatically accept the requested correlation unless one of the following restrictions applies, in which case the correlation shall be rejected: (1) The two tracks are of a different E/C, or either track has an existing E/C conflict. (2) One track is simulated and the other is live. (3) Both tracks are locally derived real-time tracks.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0065", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;After accepting a manual correlation, the C2 JU shall not subject the resulting track to automatic decorrelation processing for 5 minutes.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;correlation_type&quot;:&quot;manual&quot;}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 115, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;After acceptance of a manual correlation the resulting track shall not be the subject of automatic decorrelation processing for a period of 5 minutes.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0066", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU rejecting a requested correlation shall transmit J7.2 with the Retained/Dropped TN pair received and RV=2.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 116, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JUs rejecting the requested correlation shall initiate transmission of a J7.2 message with the Retained TN/Dropped TN set as received and RV field set to value 2.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0067", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU responding with a reverse correlation shall transmit J7.2 with the originally received Retained and Dropped TNs reversed and RV=1.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 116, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JUs responding with a reverse correlation shall transmit the J7.2 message with the originally received Retained TN and Dropped TN reversed and the RV field set to value 1.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0068", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU that does not hold the Dropped TN shall take no further action on the correlation request.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;dropped_tn_held&quot;:false}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 116, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JUs not holding the Dropped TN shall not take any further action.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0069", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If the Retained TN is not held but the Dropped TN is held and the Dropped TN has an OCC, the C2 JU shall transmit reverse correlation for RV=0, transmit rejection for RV=1, or execute correlation using Dropped TN data and Retained TN track number for RV=3.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;retained_tn_held&quot;:false,&quot;dropped_tn_held&quot;:true,&quot;dropped_tn_occ&quot;:true}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 116, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If the Retained TN is not held but the Dropped TN is held, the correlation request shall be processed as follows: (1) If the Dropped TN has an OCC, the following action shall be taken: (a) If RV is set to 0, transmit a reverse correlation with RV set to 1. (b) If RV is set to 1, transmit a correlation rejection with RV set to 2. (c) If RV is set to 3, execute the correlation using Dropped TN data and Retained TN track number.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0070", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If only the Dropped TN is held and it has no OCC, the C2 JU shall execute the correlation using Dropped TN data and the Retained TN track number.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;retained_tn_held&quot;:false,&quot;dropped_tn_held&quot;:true,&quot;dropped_tn_occ&quot;:false}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 116, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;(2) If the Dropped TN does not have an OCC, execute the correlation using Dropped TN data and Retained TN track number.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0071", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU rejecting a J7.2 while holding the Dropped TN as a local or common local track shall not interpret the J7.2 as a Drop Track message for R2 determination.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 116, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;C2 JUs rejecting a J7.2 message and holding the Dropped TN as a local or common local track shall not interpret the J7.2 message as a Drop Track message for the purpose of determining R2.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0072", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;If a received J7.2 contains one or both TNs in own unit’s in-progress J7.2 sequence and own RV is 0, 1, or 3, the C2 JU shall discontinue its own J7.2 and process the received message under rules 4.7.3.2a-h; if own RV is 2, it shall complete its in-progress sequence.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: &#x27;{&quot;tn_overlap&quot;:true}&#x27;, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 116, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;If the received J7.2 message contains one or both of the same TNs, as contained in the transmission of the own unit J7.2 message sequence in progress, the following actions shall be taken:&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}, {&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 117, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;(1) If the own unit RV field is set to value 0, 1, or 3, discontinue transmission of the own unit J7.2 message and process the received message in accordance with rules 4.7.3.2 a through h. (2) If the own unit RV field is set to value 2, complete the transmission of the message sequence in progress.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0073", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;A C2 JU shall not inhibit the J7.2 Correlation message by any filter.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;CONFIRMED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 133, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;The J7.2 Correlation message shall not be inhibited by any filter.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}, {"title": "S16-02-R0074", "html": "<pre>{&#x27;text&#x27;: &#x27;After initially achieving Active status or returning from Inactive status or TDS Failure, a C2 JU capable of assuming R2 for air or surface tracks shall not transmit tracks until R2 checks, correlation, and data registration are performed; the minimum wait is 12 seconds for air and surface tracks, with a longer 48-second land-track wait noted outside this target’s land dual-designation rules.&#x27;, &#x27;conditions&#x27;: None, &#x27;status&#x27;: &#x27;REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED&#x27;, &#x27;evidence&#x27;: [{&#x27;pdf_page_1based&#x27;: 54, &#x27;quote&#x27;: &#x27;After initially achieving Active status, or after returning to Active status from Inactive status or TDS Failure, C2 JUs capable of assuming R2 for air, surface, or land tracks shall not transmit air, surface, or land tracks until sufficient reporting responsibility checks, correlation, and data registration are performed (this also applies to a C2 JU that is deactivating a receive filter). The minimum wait before reporting air and surface tracks is 12 seconds and for land tracks is 48 seconds.&#x27;, &#x27;visual_region_description&#x27;: &#x27;&#x27;}]}</pre>"}], "repeat": false, "min_rows": 0}], "blockers": [], "requirement_meta": [{"id": "S16-02-R0001", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0002", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0003", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0004", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0005", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0006", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0007", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0008", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0009", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0010", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0011", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0012", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0013", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0014", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0015", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0016", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0017", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0018", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0019", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0020", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0021", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0022", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0023", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0024", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0025", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0026", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0027", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0028", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0029", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0030", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0031", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0032", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0033", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0034", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0035", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0036", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0037", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0038", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0039", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0040", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0041", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0042", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0043", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0044", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0045", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0046", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0047", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0048", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0049", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0050", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0051", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0052", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0053", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0054", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0055", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0056", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0057", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0058", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0059", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0060", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0061", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0062", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0063", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0064", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0065", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0066", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0067", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0068", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0069", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0070", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0071", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0072", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0073", "status": "CONFIRMED"}, {"id": "S16-02-R0074", "status": "REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED"}], "no_content": false, "material_sha256": "0c6bf5ff2198cf3d8a039c72c04c606b799f056eedae7c84ab6b8a62b3bc504a"};
